  "title": "Forum Boarium (at Pompeii)",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/garden-hortus"
  ],
  "details": "<p>This area is located at the eastern edge of the city, just inside the Porta Urbulana\u00a0(or <span>Porta</span><span>\u00a0di Sarno / Sarnus Gate)</span>, just to the north of the amphitheater. The insula was cleared between December 1954 and May 1955. W. Jashemski's work following the clearance of the <em>insula</em> demonstrated the presence of an ancient vineyard within at least a portion of it.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The so-called \"Forum Boarium\" in Pompeii was erroneously named by its 1755 excavators who discovered the bones of large bovids and assigned the name that still is used to describe this insula in Pompeii's Regio II (II, 5).",
